# Comments on generated files

When you create or substantially edit a file, leave a short comment that
a future reader (or an interviewer glancing at the header) can use.

Do:

- File-top or function-top: **what this is for** and **why it exists**
  (boundary, invariant, deliberate non-goal).
- Match the voice already in `src/lib/entropy.ts`, `flow.ts`, `validate.ts`,
  `pipeline.ts`, `worker/ai.ts` — complete sentences, not slogans.
- Point at the rule or test that locks the behaviour when there is one
  (e.g. rule 000, `entropy.test.ts`).

Do not:

- Narrate the next line (`// increment i`, `// return the result`).
- Repeat the function name in prose.
- Spray comments on every block of a file that already has a header.
- Add comments to a tiny obvious edit unless the *why* would otherwise
  be invisible.
